94e5e39f87085369c92750a7","message":"test: pin async hook halt behaviour with 2+ async onSend hooks\n\nReplying from an async `preHandler` halts the hook chain as documented\nwith zero or one async `onSend` hooks registered, but not with two or\nmore: the handler runs and overwrites the status code of a reply that\nhas already been sent, producing a response whose status and body come\nfrom different places.\n\nThe existing sibling test registers a single `onSend` hook, so the\nboundary is currently uncovered.\n\nMarked `todo` deliberately. The intended semantics are still open in\n #7090 - whether the documented halt is the contract and the hook count\nis irrelevant, or whether sending without `return reply` from an async\nhook is unsupported. This commit asserts neither; it only stops the\ndiscrepancy from living solely in an issue, so whoever picks it up\nstarts from a red test instead of re-deriving the conditions.\n\nSuite result is unchanged: fail 0, todo 1.\n\nRefs: https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/7090\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-17T10:13:43Z","author":{"name":"rokas-kve","email":"rokask1@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"rokas-kve","email":"rokask1@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":69495170,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2OTQ5NTE3MA==","name":"fastify","full_name":"fastify/fastify","private":false,"owner":{"login":"fastify","id":24939410,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI0OTM5NDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24939410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/sub